From 8eb8bc79a5050f31b099d54c722b211b070398ad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Haiyi Xu <quic_haiyix@quicinc.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Dec 2022 11:10:21 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Skip seccomp config while lxc doesn't enable seccomp

lxc 4.0.12 skip to fetch the seccomp config while lxc does not enable seccomp feature.
This will clean up the error log related with lxc.seccomp while using lxc-attach.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Haiyi Xu <quic_haiyix@quicinc.com>
---
 src/lxc/attach.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/lxc/attach.c b/src/lxc/attach.c
index 77da7bb45..5e1b96498 100644
--- a/src/lxc/attach.c
+++ b/src/lxc/attach.c
@@ -1471,8 +1471,10 @@ int lxc_attach(struct lxc_container *container, lxc_attach_exec_t exec_function,
 
 	conf = ctx->container->lxc_conf;
 
+#ifdef HAVE_SECCOMP
 	if (!fetch_seccomp(ctx->container, options))
 		WARN("Failed to get seccomp policy");
+#endif
 
 	if (!no_new_privs(ctx->container, options))
 		WARN("Could not determine whether PR_SET_NO_NEW_PRIVS is set");
-- 
2.25.1

